  "instructions": [
    {
      "id": 488331,
      "primary_message": "Cut tofu in half along the long side. Sandwich tofu between clean towels or paper towels and place on a baking sheet pan. Place a cutting board with something heavy on top and set aside to press out excess water.",
      "secondary_message": "1 (340 g) pkg extra firm tofu"
    },
    {
      "id": 488332,
      "primary_message": "Wash and dry the fresh produce.",
      "secondary_message": "½ medium head cauliflower\n1 medium zucchini squash\n½ small pkg grape tomatoes\n½ yellow bell pepper\n½ small bunch cilantro"
    },
    {
      "id": 488333,
      "primary_message": "Cut cauliflower head into quarters; using a box grater, hold the stem end of the cauliflower and coarsely grate. (Alternatively, transfer cauliflower to the bowl of a food processor; pulse until rice-like in consistency.) Place in a medium bowl and set aside. ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 488334,
      "primary_message": "Trim and quarter zucchini lengthwise, then cut crosswise into bite-sized pieces. Place in a small bowl.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 488335,
      "primary_message": "Halve tomatoes lengthwise. Add to the bowl with the zucchini. ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 488336,
      "primary_message": "Trim, seed, and medium dice bell pepper. Add to the bowl.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 488337,
      "primary_message": "Preheat a medium saucepan over medium-high heat. ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 488338,
      "primary_message": "Once the pan is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add chopped veggies and spices; cook, stirring occasionally, until veggies start to soften, about 3 minutes. ",
      "secondary_message": "1 tbsp virgin coconut oil\n1 tbsp curry powder\n2 tsp coriander, ground\n½ tsp salt\n¼ tsp black pepper"
    },
    {
      "id": 488339,
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, medium dice tofu. ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 488340,
      "primary_message": "When the veggies are softened, add coconut milk, peanut butter, sugar, chili-garlic sauce, and soy sauce to the pan. Stir to combine the curry and bring to a simmer. ",
      "secondary_message": "½ (398 ml) can coconut milk\n2 tbsp natural peanut butter\n2 tsp brown sugar\n2 tsp chili-garlic sauce\n1 tsp soy sauce"
    },
    {
      "id": 488341,
      "primary_message": "Once the curry is simmering, add tofu and stir to combine. Reduce heat to low and continue to cook, stirring occasionally, until veggies are tender and curry has thickened slightly, 8-10 minutes more. Remove from heat.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 488342,
      "primary_message": "While the curry is cooking, preheat a skillet over medium-high heat.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 488343,
      "primary_message": "Once the skillet is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add riced cauliflower, water, and salt; cook, stirring occasionally, until cauliflower is soft, about 5 minutes.",
      "secondary_message": "1 tsp virgin coconut oil\n2 tbsp water\n⅛ tsp salt"
    },
    {
      "id": 488344,
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, shave cilantro leaves off the stems; discard stems and mince the leaves.",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 488345,
      "primary_message": "When the cauliflower rice is done, remove from heat, add cilantro, and stir to combine. ",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "id": 488346,
      "primary_message": "To serve, divide cauliflower rice and curry between plates or bowls. Enjoy! ",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
